# ARK Communications Call Surfaces Lock

**Calls, missed calls, recordings, and voicemail are production-critical advisor workflows.**

Do not remove, redirect, hide from navigation, or demote these surfaces during workspace pruning, nav consolidation, or "simplification" passes — **unless the user explicitly asks**, or the change is a **documented upgrade** that preserves or improves the same operational jobs.

## Protected surfaces

| Surface | Route | Job |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Calls & VM** | `operations.communications.calls` | Who called, missed calls, recordings, voicemail playback, mark handled, notes |
| **CallSession authority** | — | Telephony truth; not replaced by Attention rows alone |
| **Comms section nav link** | Calls & VM in `section-nav.blade.php` | Advisors must discover the call library without memorizing URLs |

Related and also protected from silent removal:

- Needs Attention (calls lane / live interrupt path)
- Inbox / History (when restored — do not re-collapse into Attention without observation)
- Topbar Calls Waiting / comms interrupt for live calls

## Forbidden without explicit request

- Removing **Calls & VM** from Communications section nav
- Redirecting `/app/communications/calls` to Attention or Inbox
- Deleting or hiding voicemail/recording playback UI
- Assuming Attention "Calls lane" replaces the dedicated call library

## Allowed

- Upgrading playback, filters, or CallSession metadata **on the same route**
- Observation-gated merges **after** floor evidence — not audit speculation
- Redirecting true duplicates (e.g. legacy workboard → Attention) when the job is identical

## Prune pass rule

Workspace surface audits may label call library "borderline" or "Phase 2." **That is not permission to remove it.** Borderline means observe usage — not delete navigation in Phase 1.

When in doubt: **keep the call surface visible.**
